## API FUNDAMENTALS

### Base URL
https://{{PVE_HOST}}:8006/api2/json/

All endpoints are prefixed with /api2/json/. The root tree exposes:
/cluster, /nodes, /storage, /access, /pools

### Two Authentication Methods

#### Method A — API Token (PREFERRED for automation)
Stateless. No CSRF needed for writes. Tokens can be scoped below their parent user's privileges.

Header format:
  Authorization: PVEAPIToken=USER@REALM!TOKENID=UUID

Example:
  Authorization: PVEAPIToken=automation@pve!deploy=aaaaaaaaa-bbbb-cccc-dddd-ef0123456789

Token format decoded:
- USER     = Proxmox username (e.g. automation, root)
- REALM    = auth realm (pam = Linux PAM, pve = Proxmox built-in)
- TOKENID  = name you gave the token at creation
- UUID     = the secret value shown once at creation

#### Method B — Ticket (session-based)
Requires CSRF header on all write operations (POST/PUT/DELETE). Tickets expire ~2 hours.

  Step 1 — Authenticate:
    curl -k -X POST \
      -d 'username=root@pam' \
      --data-urlencode 'password=SECRET' \
      https://{{PVE_HOST}}:8006/api2/json/access/ticket

  Response:
    { "data": { "ticket": "PVE:root@pam:...", "CSRFPreventionToken": "4EEC61E2:..." } }

  Step 2 — GET with cookie:
    curl -k -H 'Cookie: PVEAuthCookie=PVE:root@pam:...' \
      https://{{PVE_HOST}}:8006/api2/json/nodes

  Step 3 — POST/PUT/DELETE — add CSRF header:
    curl -k -X POST \
      -H 'Cookie: PVEAuthCookie=PVE:root@pam:...' \
      -H 'CSRFPreventionToken: 4EEC61E2:...' \
      -d 'vmid=101&...' \
      https://{{PVE_HOST}}:8006/api2/json/nodes/pve/qemu

RULE: Always prefer API tokens for automation. Tokens bypass CSRF requirements entirely.

