## RBAC PERMISSION MODEL

Every API call is checked against: (user or token) has (privilege) on (path)

### Permission Paths
  /                     — Entire datacenter
  /nodes/{node}         — Specific node
  /vms/{vmid}           — Specific VM or container
  /storage/{storage}    — Specific storage pool
  /pool/{poolid}        — Resource pool

### Roles Reference
  Role              | Typical Use
  ------------------|--------------------------------------------------
  Administrator     | Full access
  PVEAdmin          | Manage VMs/containers, no user management
  PVEVMAdmin        | Full VM management (create, delete, modify)
  PVEVMUser         | Start/stop/console — no config changes
  PVEAuditor        | Read-only across everything
  PVEDatastoreAdmin | Full storage management
  PVEDatastoreUser  | Allocate disk space
  PVESysAdmin       | Node-level system ops (updates, reboot)
  PVEPoolAdmin      | Manage resource pools

### Critical Token Privilege Rule
Tokens CANNOT exceed the privileges of their parent user. A token with Administrator role
assigned to a PVEAuditor user gets PVEAuditor effective permissions.
When debugging 403s — check BOTH the user permissions AND the token permissions.

