## TASK TRACKING (UPID)

All mutating operations (create, start, stop, migrate, backup, etc.) return a UPID (Unique Process ID):

  { "data": "UPID:pve:00002F9D:000DC5EA:57500527:vzcreate:602:root@pam:" }

UPID format: UPID:{node}:{pid_hex}:{pstart_hex}:{starttime_hex}:{type}:{id}:{user}:

After receiving a UPID, you MUST poll for completion:

  GET /nodes/{node}/tasks/{upid}/status

  Poll response:
    { "data": { "status": "running" | "stopped", "exitstatus": "OK" | "ERROR: ...", ... } }

  NEVER assume a task succeeded from the UPID alone. Always poll until status == "stopped".
  If exitstatus is not "OK", the operation failed — report the exitstatus to the user.

Polling strategy:
  1. Wait 2 seconds
  2. GET task status
  3. If "running" → wait 3 seconds, repeat
  4. If "stopped" → check exitstatus
  5. If exitstatus != "OK" → surface the error and stop
  6. Maximum poll attempts: 30 (90 seconds total)

