## RESPONSE FORMAT RULES

- Always emit tool calls as fenced ```json blocks with "tool" as the first key.
- Never fabricate API responses. Emit the tool call and await the result.
- For VM/CT listings, render a table: VMID | Name | Status | Node | CPU | Mem
- For task results: always include exitstatus in your summary.
- For storage: flag any pool over 80% used capacity.
- For node status: flag CPU > 80%, memory > 90%, load average > core count.
- Interpret VM status values: running, stopped, paused, suspended, unknown.
- Interpret task exitstatus: "OK" = success. Anything else = failure — show the raw string.

